[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
How each requirement in ``docs/requirements/mobile/`` is verified. Automated tests run with ``flutter test`` in ``mobile_app/``.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: AI buddy

[VERIFICATION]
UID: VER-MOB-001
METHOD: Test
TITLE: AI buddy tab follows the backend
STATEMENT: >>>
The tab count follows the backend status, and an open AI buddy tab falls back to Agenda when it disappears.
<<<
TEST: >>>
mobile_app/test/ai_buddy_test.dart: only shown while the backend has the AI buddy configured, an open AI buddy tab falls back to Agenda when it disappears
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The widget layout of the navigation is not covered: the app cannot be pumped in widget tests (CLAUDE.md).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-050
  ROLE: Verifies

[VERIFICATION]
UID: VER-MOB-002
METHOD: Test
TITLE: Chat shows the conversation
STATEMENT: >>>
The conversation is loaded from the backend and a sent message is followed by the answer, both with the backend's ids and times.
<<<
TEST: >>>
mobile_app/test/ai_buddy_test.dart: loads the conversation from the backend, shows the message and the typing state while waiting, parses the backend message format
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Bubble layout is checked by hand on a phone.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-051
  ROLE: Verifies

[VERIFICATION]
UID: VER-MOB-003
METHOD: Test
TITLE: Typing state while waiting
STATEMENT: >>>
While the answer is pending the chat state is 'sending', which shows the typing bubble and disables sending.
<<<
TEST: >>>
mobile_app/test/ai_buddy_test.dart: shows the message and the typing state while waiting
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-052
  ROLE: Verifies

[VERIFICATION]
UID: VER-MOB-004
METHOD: Test
TITLE: Failed messages can be sent again
STATEMENT: >>>
An offline failure keeps the message with a Dutch error; retrying sends the same text and shows the answer.
<<<
TEST: >>>
mobile_app/test/ai_buddy_test.dart: a failed message shows the error and can be sent again
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-053
  ROLE: Verifies

[VERIFICATION]
UID: VER-MOB-005
METHOD: Test
TITLE: Reload after answers
STATEMENT: >>>
Every answer bumps the refresh signal the agenda and task screens listen to; a failure does not.
<<<
TEST: >>>
mobile_app/test/ai_buddy_test.dart: every answer asks the agenda and task screens to reload, a failed message does not trigger a reload
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-054
  ROLE: Verifies

[VERIFICATION]
UID: VER-MOB-006
METHOD: Test
TITLE: Clear the conversation
STATEMENT: >>>
Clearing empties the conversation in the app and on the backend.
<<<
TEST: >>>
mobile_app/test/ai_buddy_test.dart: clearing empties the conversation on the backend
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-055
  ROLE: Verifies

[VERIFICATION]
UID: VER-MOB-007
METHOD: Test
TITLE: Voice input fills the text field
STATEMENT: >>>
With a fake speech service: the microphone shows only while the text field is empty and no answer is awaited; listening shows partial text in the field; stopping keeps the final text without sending it; nothing recognised leaves the field empty; refused permission and missing speech recognition give the Dutch messages.
<<<
TEST: >>>
mobile_app/test/ai_voice_test.dart: microphone only on an empty field, partial results fill the field, final text is kept and not sent, nothing recognised leaves the field empty, refused permission shows a message, no speech recognition shows a message
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-056
  ROLE: Verifies

[VERIFICATION]
UID: VER-MOB-008
METHOD: Demonstration
TITLE: Voice input on a phone
STATEMENT: >>>
On an Android phone: the first tap asks for microphone permission; speaking Dutch shows the text while speaking; recognition stops after a pause; the text can be changed and sent.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The real speech recognition service and the permission dialog only exist on a device, so this part cannot run in flutter test.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-056
  ROLE: Verifies

[VERIFICATION]
UID: VER-MOB-009
METHOD: Test
TITLE: Sending voice messages automatically
STATEMENT: >>>
The setting is off by default and survives a restart; when on, the final recognised text is sent once recognition stops, and nothing recognised sends nothing; when off, nothing is sent.
<<<
TEST: >>>
mobile_app/test/ai_voice_test.dart: auto-send is off by default and is stored, auto-send sends the final text, auto-send with nothing recognised sends nothing
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-057
  ROLE: Verifies

